@*
    WizardShell — shared page-frame primitive for the six wizards. M.2d.1
    deliverable per the v2 plan §5.1.

    Responsibilities (narrow by design — round-1 #1 in the M.2d.1 review):
      * Header band — back-arrow + protocol icon + title + subtitle.
      * Load-state guard — Loading / Error / Content branches.
      * ChildContent slot — sections, banners, anything the wizard arranges.
      * Footer slot — typically a WizardActions row.
      * SaveState parameter — passthrough only; no visual side-effect in
        M.2d.1 (Q4 lock).

    What this is NOT responsible for (anti-coupling locks):
      * Section structure — WizardSection owns numbered cards.
      * Layout — wizards decide MudGrid / table / flex / etc. inside
        WizardSection.ChildContent.
      * Save-state visualisation — M.2d.2/.3 decide per-wizard.
      * Validation anchoring — WizardValidationBanner owns the surface;
        scroll/focus implementation lands in M.2d.4.
      * Runtime Tap behaviour — WizardWatchSlot owns the embed.

    DoD §6 anti-coupling check: this file contains zero
    MudPaper-with-numbered-title constructs.

    Reference: docs/sessions/2026-05-21-m2d1-shared-primitives-plan-v2.md §5.1
*@

@* page-heading is the Studio-wide sticky heading band (site.css §Page heading).
   Every other screen carries it; without it the wizard title scrolls away and
   the operator loses track of which wizard they are in on a tall form.

   Suppressed when Embedded: the host (the onboarding overlay) already titles the
   panel, so rendering this produced two stacked headers — "Configure Modbus TCP"
   above "Add Modbus TCP source" — saying the same thing twice. ADR-0016 Rule 3
   gives the heading to the host in embedded mode. *@
@if (!Embedded)
{
<MudStack Row="true" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Spacing="2" Class="mb-4 page-heading">
    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(BackHref))
    {
        <MudTooltip Text="Back">
            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ArrowBack"
                           OnClick="@OnBackClicked"
                           Size="Size.Small"
                           aria-label="Back to the previous screen" />
        </MudTooltip>
    }
    @if (Icon is not null)
    {
        <MudIcon Icon="@Icon" Size="Size.Medium" Color="Color.Primary" />
    }
    <div>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Title))
        {
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5">@Title</MudText>
        }
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Subtitle))
        {
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">@Subtitle</MudText>
        }
        @* Progress ("Step 3 of 5 — Upload CSV") belongs WITH the title that names
           the wizard, not in a card of its own above the content: a card is a
           place where work happens, and a step counter is not work.

           A RenderFragment rather than a string so the caller owns the pill's
           visual — the shell has no stylesheet hook of its own here, and a
           caller-supplied MudChip renders as a pill without needing one. *@
        @if (HeaderMeta is not null)
        {
            <div class="mt-1" data-testid="wizard-shell-meta">@HeaderMeta</div>
        }
    </div>
</MudStack>
}

@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(LoadError))
{
    <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Error" Variant="Variant.Outlined" Class="mb-4" data-testid="wizard-shell-load-error">
        <strong>Could not load.</strong> @LoadError
    </MudAlert>
}
else if (IsLoading)
{
    <MudProgressLinear Color="Color.Primary" Indeterminate="true" data-testid="wizard-shell-loading" />
}
else
{
    <div data-testid="wizard-shell-content">
        @ChildContent
    </div>

    @* Embedded wizards hide their WizardActions per ADR-0016 Rule 3, but the
       RenderFragment is still non-null, so this wrapper used to paint an empty
       bordered strip at the foot of the overlay. The host supplies the actions. *@
    @if (Footer is not null && !Embedded)
    {
        @* Pins Save / Cancel / Test to the foot of the scroll region so they stay
           reachable on a tall form — the Modbus RTU wizard with its serial fields
           is the worst case. On a short form it sits in normal flow at the end of
           the content. See .sticky-action-bar in site.css for why its offset is 0
           rather than the status-footer height. *@
        <div data-testid="wizard-shell-footer" class="sticky-action-bar">
            @Footer
        </div>
    }
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Protocol-specific icon for the header band.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Icon { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Header title text.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Header subtitle text.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Subtitle { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Optional short progress marker rendered beneath the subtitle — e.g. a
    /// <c>Step 3 of 5 — Upload CSV</c> pill for a multi-step wizard. Omit for
    /// single-page wizards, where nothing is rendered.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? HeaderMeta { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Parent route the back-arrow navigates to (e.g. <c>/sources/new</c>).
    /// When null or empty, the back arrow is hidden.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? BackHref { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Optional explicit back-click handler. If null, the shell navigates
    /// via the injected <c>NavigationManager</c> to <see cref="BackHref"/>.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnBack { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// True when this wizard is rendered inside another surface (the
    /// Connect-a-device overlay). Suppresses the shell's own heading band and
    /// action-bar wrapper so the host owns both — ADR-0016 Rule 3.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Embedded { get; set; }

    /// <summary>True while the wizard is loading its initial config.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool IsLoading { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Non-null/non-empty: render the load-error branch.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? LoadError { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The body of the wizard — WizardSection instances + validation
    /// banners + anything else the wizard arranges. Layout is the
    /// wizard's choice.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Optional footer slot. Typically a <c>WizardActions</c> instance.
    /// Renders nothing when null.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Footer { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Save-state passthrough — M.2d.1 exposes the parameter; M.2d.2/.3
    /// decide whether to render a chip, toast, or nothing per the Q4
    /// verdict. No visual side-effect inside the shell itself.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public WizardSaveState SaveState { get; set; } = WizardSaveState.Editing;

    [Inject] private NavigationManager Nav { get; set; } = default!;

    private async Task OnBackClicked()
    {
        if (OnBack.HasDelegate)
        {
            await OnBack.InvokeAsync();
        }
        else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(BackHref))
        {
            Nav.NavigateTo(BackHref);
        }
    }
}
